    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ)_\n\nFollow-up to #294.\n\n## What\n\n**Emacs (Linux/Windows, `sp-text-manipulation`)**\n- `s-c` is translated to `C-c` and `s-x` to `C-x` (`key-translation-map`), so Super carries the prefixes: `s-c C-c` = `C-c C-c`, `s-x C-f` = `C-x C-f`.\n- A typed `C-c` / `C-x` that starts a key sequence becomes copy / cut (private events `<sp-copy>`, `<sp-cut>`). Inside a sequence they keep their stock meaning. This replaces the `C-S-c` / `C-S-x` from #294.\n- On Windows `w32-lwindow-modifier` / `w32-rwindow-modifier` are `super`.\n- Mac is unchanged.\n\n**i3 and sway (options for freeing Super)**\n- Chosen: Caps Lock becomes the Level 3 shift (`lv3:caps_switch`, Mod5) and `$mod` is `Mod5`. Nothing binds Mod4 any more, so the Windows key reaches Emacs. Same physical layer key as AeroSpace on the Mac.\n- Other options, not taken: `caps:hyper` (Hyper often shares Mod4 in X, so it may not free Super); Alt as `$mod` (clashes with Meta, which Sia reserved for Emacs); Ctrl+Alt chords (awkward, and Ctrl+Alt is used by terminals/Emacs).\n- Caveat of the choice: Caps+letter yields AltGr-level characters on layouts that have them, but the WM grabs bound combinations first.\n\n**Docs**\n- `sp-keys.org`: new section \"Replaced prefixes and chords\" with a table of stock key vs Mac vs Linux/Windows, and how to look up a key (`C-h k`, `C-h w`).\n- Top-level `README.org`: note that most keys are bound differently, pointing to that table.\n- `sp-text-manipulation.org` and `global-keymap-namespaces.org` updated, with the caveats (Windows takes `Win+C` / `Win+X`; needs a remap).\n\n## Not run\n\nNo Emacs, i3 or sway in the container. The \"starts a sequence\" check uses `this-command-keys-vector` from memory; try `C-h k s-c C-c`, `C-h k C-c`, `C-c C-c` in Org, and `lv3:caps_switch` + `$mod` in i3/sway. No CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAZg8pR9NBT6MCe97U)_",
